tStore.read`, `EventStore.save_snapshot`)**:\n  - `append(stream_id, events, expected_version)`:\n    - Reject non-int/bool or mismatched `expected_version` (`type(expected_version) is not int or expected_version != current`) with `ConflictError(\"expected version does not match\")` before consuming or mutating anything (currently uses `\u003e` instead of `!=`, failing to reject `\u003c current`).\n    - Materialize and validate the entire batch before mutating state: for each item, check `isinstance(raw, Event)`, deep-copy it (`ev = deepcopy(raw)`), run `ev.__post_init__()`, and assign `ev.stream_version = current + offset` (1-based offset). Never mutate caller `Event` instances.\n    - Append deep-copied batch to `self._streams.setdefault(stream_id, [])` when non-empty, and return `deepcopy(batch)` so mutating returned events or their nested payloads cannot corrupt stored stream state.\n  - `read(stream_id, after_version=0)`:\n    - Validate `type(after_version) is int and after_version \u003e= 0`, else raise `ValueError(\"invalid version\")`.\n    - Return `deepcopy(self._streams.get(stream_id, [])[after_version:])` so caller mutations to returned events/payloads never affect stored events.\n  - `save_snapshot(stream_id, version, state)`:\n    - Validate `type(version) is int and 0 \u003c= version \u003c= self.version(stream_id)` and `isinstance(state, dict)`, else raise `ValueError(\"invalid snapshot\")`.\n    - Store `{\"version\": version, \"state\": deepcopy(state)}`.\n- **`projector.py` (`replay`)**:\n  - In `replay(store, stream_id, use_snapshot=True)`, pass `after_version=version` to `store.read(stream_id, after_version=version)` (currently hardcoded to `after_version=0`, which re-applies already-snapshotted events).\n\n### Verify Command\n`pytest -q --tb=short`\n","duration_seconds":28.290223,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":4545,"output_tokens":1450,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":44689,"total_tokens":5995}}}
